  "version": 1,
  "title": "Rational Recovery on a Common Ruler",
  "abstract": "For the rational plane curve parametrization x ↦ ((x-1)/x^n, (x-1)^2/(x-K)^m) with real K>1 and integers n,m at least two, the index of its coordinate field in R(x) is one except at (n,m,K)=(2,4,2), where it is two. In the exceptional case the involution x ↦ x/(x-1) preserves both coordinates.",
